      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Staying hydrated and eating won’t protect your kidneys or prevent the increased bleeding risk from that high a dose—those safeguards mainly help with mild stomach upset, not the serious dangers. At 800mg every 4 hours, you’d be taking 4,800mg daily, which is well above the 3,200mg max and can cause acute kidney injury or gastrointestinal bleeding even in healthy people. If you absolutely must push through, stick to 800mg every 6 hours (3,200mg/day) for no more than 2–3 days, and set alarms so you don’t accidentally take more. But honestly, a quick call to your doctor or pharmacist could get you a safer prescription option that works faster and longer.",
